<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Cultures</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Cultures of Oceania</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 3 cultures of Oceania, from the Aboriginal Australians to the Māori. Read their profiles, then answer.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Oceania">Open the cultures &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the cultures from 1 (the earliest to begin) to 3 (the latest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Lapita culture</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Māori</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Aboriginal Australians</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right homeland next to each culture. Their profiles will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Aboriginal Australians</li><li>Lapita culture</li><li>Māori</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The Australian mainland, Tasmania and many islands, excluding the Torres Strait Islands</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>New Zealand (Aotearoa), above all the North Island</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>The western Pacific, from the Bismarck Archipelago of Papua New Guinea through the Reef and Santa Cruz…</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p><b>Aboriginal Australians</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The ancestors of Aboriginal Australians reached Sahul, the land that joined Australia and New Guinea, 50,000 to 65,000 years ago, and may have settled across the continent within 6,000 years of landing.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Lapita culture</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The Lapita culture, named after a site in New Caledonia and known by its finely stamped pottery, appeared in the Bismarck Archipelago north-east of New Guinea between about 1500 and 1300 BCE.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p><b>Māori</b>. Its profile says: &#8220;The ancestors of the Māori sailed from eastern Polynesia in ocean-going waka and settled New Zealand around 1250–1350, last of all the Polynesian lands.&#8221; Find one piece of evidence on the profile for this, and say how we know it.</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose two of these cultures that lived at the same time. What did they have in common, and what set them apart?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/profiles?kind=culture&amp;region=Oceania. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Cultures of Oceania</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the cultures in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Aboriginal Australians <span>c. 63000 BCE to today</span></li><li>Lapita culture <span>c. 1500 BCE – c. 500 BCE</span></li><li>Māori <span>c. 1300 CE to today</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Match the cultures to their homelands</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Aboriginal Australians <span>1: The Australian mainland, Tasmania and many islands, excluding the Torres Strait Islands</span></li><li>Lapita culture <span>3: The western Pacific, from the Bismarck Archipelago of Papua New Guinea through the Reef and Santa Cruz…</span></li><li>Māori <span>2: New Zealand (Aotearoa), above all the North Island</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers use details from the profiles.</p></section></div></details>
